/static/chunks/0taliq9wft957.js\\\",\\\"/_next/static/chunks/3ppkpjc789k8m.js\\\"],\\\"Image\\\"]\\n21:T1b0e,\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"Shri Bhuvan Parshwanath and Shri Bhidbhanjan Parshwanath. 14. Shri Bhuvan Parshwanath. Main Deity: A beautifully adorned black-hued idol of Shri Bhuvan Parshwanath in the padmasana posture, 27 inches tall and 22 inches wide, complete with an ornate parikar (surrounding frame). Above the idol's head is a canopy of seven serpent hoods.. Location: This temple is located in Bhoyara Padha in the city of Khambhat, Gujarat.. History: The ancient name of Khambhat was \\\"Trambavati,\\\" and today it is known in English as \\\"Cambay.\\\" Since ancient times Khambhat has been very famous for its Jain temples. This temple of Parshwanath is known as the \\\"Navkhand Parshwanath Temple.\\\" This Navkhand Parshwanath is also known as \\\"Bhuvan Parshwanath.\\\" A mention of this is found in the preface of the book \\\"Jaytihun Stotra\\\" by Shri Girdharlal Hirabai. This idol of Shri Bhuvan Parshwanath attracts, delights, and captivates the eyes of devotees. The temple bears an inscription stating that the idol of Lord Ajitnath was consecrated here by Shri Harivijaysurishwarji in V.S. 1636, which attests to the antiquity of this temple. This temple was renovated in V.S. 2027, with the Mulanayak idols kept in their original places. Every year the temple flag is hoisted on the fifth day of the bright half of the month of Vaishakh. Several scriptures inscribed on copper plates are preserved here in the knowledge repository (gyan bhandar).. Other Temples: There are four other temples in Bhoyara Padha - 1. Shri Shantinath-Neminath Temple, 2. Shri Shantinath Temple, which contains an ancient and appealing idol of Parshwanath inscribed with V.S. 1383 (the other idols in this temple date from the 16th century), 3. Shri Mallinath Swami Temple, 4. Shri Chandraprabhu Swami Temple. Khambhat has more than 74 temples, which are the pride of Gujarat.. Directions: Khambhat is 80 km from Vadodara and 90 km from Ahmedabad. Khambhat has several dharamshalas and bhojanshalas. There are many upashrayas, pathshalas (religious schools), and gyan bhandars (knowledge repositories) here, preserving many ancient manuscripts and idols.. Scripture References: Many scriptures, verses (shlokas), and ras compositions were written here by the great acharyas, monks, and others of this region. The \\\"Shri Gautam Swami Ras\\\" was written in Khambhat by Shri Vinayaprabhaji in V.S. 1422. In the mid-16th century, Shri Nansurji wrote \\\"Vichar Sogath,\\\" \\\"Gajsukumar Rajarshi Sajjaya,\\\" and \\\"Panch Tirth Stavan.\\\" In V.S. 1567, Shri Lavanya Samay wrote \\\"Surpriya Kevali Ras.\\\" In V.S. 1642, Shri Vacharajji wrote \\\"Samyaktva Komudi Ras\\\" and \\\"Shri Shantinath Charitra.\\\" Shri Sakalchandra Upadhyay wrote \\\"Shri Vasupujya Jin Punya Prakash Ras\\\" in V.S. 1643. Shri Kushalabhji wrote \\\"Shri Satambhan Parshwanath Stavan\\\" in V.S. 1653. In the 17th century Shri Rishabhdasji wrote several works in Gujarati. During his chaturmas (monsoon retreat) here in V.S. 1727, Shri Labhvijayji wrote \\\"Shripal Mayasundari Ras.\\\" Shri Bhanuvijayji wrote \\\"Maun Ekadasi Stavan\\\" and \\\"Shashwata Ashwasata Jin Tirthmala\\\" in V.S. 1773. In the 18th century Shri Yashovijayji wrote \\\"Sadhu Vandana,\\\" \\\"Maun Ekadasi 150 Kalyanak Stavan,\\\" \\\"Jambo Ras,\\\" and other works. Shri Matisagarji wrote \\\"Khambhat ki Tirthmala\\\" and \\\"Dhanna Rishi Chaupai.\\\" Shri Atmaramji Maharaj wrote \\\"Agyan Timir Bhaskar\\\" in V.S. 1942.. The main temple of Shri Bhuvan Parshwanath is located in Bhoyara Padha in Khambhat. Shri Bhuvan Parshwanath is also known as Shri Navkhand Parshwanath, and there are several temples dedicated to Shri Navkhand Parshwanath throughout India.. Hymn of Praise: O Bhuvan Parshwanath, ocean of virtuous gems, enchanter of the world, the gods themselves are entranced by the beauty of your image. Take my hand, O Lord, and lead me up the steps to liberation. With loving devotion I bow to Shri Bhuvan Parshwa.. Chanting Mantra: Om Hrim Arham Shri Bhuvan Parshwanathaya Namah.. Trust: Shri Bhuvan Parshwanath Shwetambar Jain Tirth, Bhoyara Padha, Post: Khambhat, District: Anand, Gujarat - 388620, Phone: 02698-223780.. History of the 108 Lords Parshwanath and How to Reach Them - Part 5: After completing the pilgrimage to Navsari, the four temples of Surat and Rander, the two temples of Bharuch and Gandhar, the four temples of Dabhoi, Chhani, and Borsad, and the four temples of Khambhat - a total of 14 pilgrimage sites of Lord Parshwanath - we will next travel to the two Parshwanath pilgrimage sites of Kheda and Dholka. From Khambhat to Kheda is 56 km, and from Khambhat to the Dholka pilgrimage site is 30 km. In Kheda is the 15th site, Shri Bhidbhanjan Parshwanath, and in Dholka is the 16th site, Shri Kalikund Parshwanath.. 15. Shri Bhidbhanjan Parshwanath. Main Deity: A white-stone idol of Lord Shri Bhidbhanjan Parshwanath in the padmasana posture, 25 inches tall and 21 inches wide.. Location: This temple is in Patel Padha in the town of Kheda, on the Ahmedabad-Bombay National Highway.. History: Once, Acharya Shri Vijayraj was on his way to the town of Kheda when, along the way, near the village of Hariyala, he sat down to meditate beneath a banyan tree. Word spread that a great soul (mahatma) had arrived by the riverside outside the village. The villagers gathered to have his darshan. At that time the acharya was seated in meditation. The villagers were deeply impressed by the radiance on his face. When the acharya emerged from meditation and saw the simplicity of the villagers and the eagerness of the people, he preached to them the virtues of Jainism and inspired them to embrace it. The villagers became Jains and took Jain vows from the acharya. The devotees then asked for a Jain idol for worship. Hearing this, the acharya asked them to dig at the very spot where he had been sitting, beneath the banyan tree. While digging, they found a beautiful and majestic idol, two kayotsarga (standing-meditation) images, a brass lamp-stand, and a copper vessel. Seeing the radiance of the Lord's image, the people were overjoyed. In Vikram Samvat year 1516, a Jain temple was built by the riverbank, and the smiling image of Shri Bhidbhanjan Parshwanath was installed there. This idol is believed to date from the era of King Samprati. It is believed that worshipping this image removes the difficulties of devotees. This idol dates from the 5th century, and the temple still stands today in the town of Kheda. This temple was renovated in V.S. 1794, and its most recent renovation was completed in Vikram Samvat 2053. This is the birthplace of Upadhyay Shri Udayratnaji and Acharya Shri Kapoorsurishwarji. Holy days such as Kartik Purnima and Chaitra Purnima hold special significance at this temple.. Other Temples: In addition, there are eight temples in Kheda district.. Art and Sculptural Work: Since this idol dates from the time of King Samprati, its artistry is extraordinary and wondrous. Recovered from the ground in the kayotsarga posture, this idol is delightful to behold.\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"1b:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mb-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"a\\\",null,{\\\"href\\\":\\\"https://goo.gl/maps/p4R11Pc8KZERsNet5\\\",\\\"target\\\":\\\"_blank\\\",\\\"rel\\\":\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-sm bg-maroon px-5 py-2.5 font-ui text-sm font-medium text-ivory hover:bg-maroon-deep transition-colors\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$L1a\\\",null,{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"$undefined\\\",\\\"iconNode\\\":\\\"$8:2:props:children:props:children:1:props:children:0:props:iconNode\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"lucide-map-pin h-4 w-4\\\",\\\"aria-hidden\\\":true}],\\\"Open in Google Maps\\\"]}],null,[\\\"$\\\",\\